#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2 ,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067400/assets/94484d767cbf92566de8b73fdbd887ea2da85fbf1dd9f3daf9a0c9ea73608d4b.png)\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,x-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=1} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197950 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩|}_{x=1+2u+v\\,y=u+v\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (-2)+(1+2u+v)\\cdot 3+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+2v+3+6u+3v+u+v \\\\  & =5u+6v+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[5uv+3{v}^{2}+3v]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5u+6)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}+6u]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10+12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888ad587-c5a4-5a4a-b25e-23442b9f6145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4uv^{3} + 2u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193974} {:answer/id #uuid "12cb63f6-04da-555f-b2ff-3767b04d83b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193975} {:answer/id #uuid "36224e2f-542c-560b-bc8f-0fbe2b8bad7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8uv^{3} + 8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193976} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad24b67-d3ee-5cf3-9c87-49b1335fbe0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8uv^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193977} {:answer/id #uuid "6377b499-7d79-55e4-8846-6c9884bf45b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv^{3} + 4u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cb63f6-04da-555f-b2ff-3767b04d83b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193975} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a445eba-94eb-5e71-9f27-e1e0696f19ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956510e3-0ede-564b-a4f8-7f3698f007f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193980} {:answer/id #uuid "cd73118b-cac4-5f69-a0de-54bbfa2a44a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193981} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab3018e-5d19-59b1-a01c-c67ddcca9c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193982} {:answer/id #uuid "366f8bbe-0903-53e7-93da-9d71aab6f2fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193983} {:answer/id #uuid "78522f09-5858-5e3d-b17a-1cd32ae40b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "956510e3-0ede-564b-a4f8-7f3698f007f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193980} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc620df2-8885-5b7a-8f11-c8d0842232eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186193979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69fe42a1-24c6-5f53-90f3-883e2fa5e193" :question/math-academy-id "q-160845" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-1,\\,2v,\\,2-3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩|}_{x=u-1\\,y=2v\\,z=2-3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3(u-1)+(2v)+(2-3u-2v),\\,\\frac{2v}{2}-2,\\,-3(u-1)-(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6+(v-2)\\cdot 2+(2v+1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6+2v-4+4v+2 \\\\  & =6v-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[u]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [3{v}^{2}-8v]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abb611fa-739f-583c-a2ea-e0822cdfcd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194016} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a9a67-3b47-5c59-bd22-6a5d8be8e186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194017} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8c84ae-9834-5e26-898c-a0a5cddaa6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194018} {:answer/id #uuid "ded35ada-3577-58d8-be4d-f436da7fb349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194019} {:answer/id #uuid "13ad414e-c611-536a-b4a7-a5f624ac5dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a9a67-3b47-5c59-bd22-6a5d8be8e186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194017} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1759a5-2eaa-5374-85aa-575bbdf9ae30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6b5a3a2-513f-5721-bf54-260cfc8a8f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160886" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-1,\\,uv,\\,3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩|}_{x=2u-1\\,y=uv\\,z=3v} \\\\  & =⟨2(2u-1),\\,\\frac{(2u-1)(3v)}{3}-2uv,\\,2(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\cdot ⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =(4u-2)\\cdot 3v+(-v)\\cdot (-6)+6v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =12uv-6v+6v+12uv \\\\  & =24uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}24uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}[12{u}^{2}v]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}12v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[6{v}^{2}]_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =6({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaf3fb00-efdd-557e-ae5e-23220f3035eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}v+u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354988} {:answer/id #uuid "e874e9d6-833e-5363-9472-51851d9246d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354989} {:answer/id #uuid "488423e1-a1f3-53b3-9177-3a9a567b2dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354990} {:answer/id #uuid "38278083-5efb-5880-926a-5ba6ad1bae35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{u}^{3}v-2u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354991} {:answer/id #uuid "fb54cc54-2c00-5d02-a9a1-62f3a13fc928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "488423e1-a1f3-53b3-9177-3a9a567b2dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354990} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9340e53-1d71-5a0d-b92a-db3e7ce81ead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac672908-2a28-5387-88a2-598e1fa02dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161249" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,-uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-uv\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+(-2uv)\\cdot (-4uv)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+8{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40dbeeeb-9778-53ec-a86e-d16b3d02f826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354995} {:answer/id #uuid "18389183-d18d-5f72-9502-24ff506519a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354996} {:answer/id #uuid "ed010834-2acf-5378-beae-c9860f5240aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354997} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3e6519-24a8-5516-8ed4-db8128e00666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354998} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb7b720-69b1-5e69-9ffb-4ada04a295d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe3e6519-24a8-5516-8ed4-db8128e00666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354998} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9006772-216e-59b7-bbde-e629d5c41e4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50f21d4c-115f-5f6b-a6fe-50fa77f7169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161251" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)+3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)+{u}^{2}\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡v+{sin}^{2}⁡v)+{u}^{3} \\\\  & =-5{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,-5{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853c8197-5b44-5084-96d4-7bc289633d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355002} {:answer/id #uuid "eb116170-4f12-55bc-b24c-b364339c8a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355003} {:answer/id #uuid "f9068ec7-62dc-5c52-b935-f133bb52e471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355004} {:answer/id #uuid "c73c01d6-cb4c-55a2-b83f-9f2f0a2cce7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355005} {:answer/id #uuid "ab403fe9-701a-50cf-b39c-88efc7bdf023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb116170-4f12-55bc-b24c-b364339c8a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355003} :answer-field/id #uuid "73ad2581-bd99-5553-95d9-ec556502ae12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "247c04ba-ae19-5fb9-8ad9-13cb102acf1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161262" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3u{v}^{2},\\,u-v,\\,2⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩|}_{x=3u{v}^{2}\\,y=u-v\\,z=2} \\\\  & =⟨{(3u{v}^{2})}^{2},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =9{u}^{2}{v}^{4}\\cdot 0+(3u{v}^{2}+u-v)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-6uv-3{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[u{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(u+\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}u]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6(-2+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2462b850-5a89-5fa5-9690-50653c3eb427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355009} {:answer/id #uuid "94a2bc5a-0e6d-549c-a6ff-34951a49b142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355010} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7596e7-f0b3-5996-a1d8-f4e761c87e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355011} {:answer/id #uuid "66b44f04-000e-52c2-8487-cad6fadcff2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355012} {:answer/id #uuid "06b3fe65-598a-5d15-8ba3-f65cfe126e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f7596e7-f0b3-5996-a1d8-f4e761c87e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355011} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec5800a-fbe3-5aba-89a9-6ae9aea1a7ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba1436a2-8021-58b2-945f-5a403da2e963" :question/math-academy-id "q-161263" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-v)+uv\\cdot (-2{u}^{2})+v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-3uv-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4}v+{u}^{2}v]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[-3{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3a8a40f-1824-53a6-9057-3d354d424fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355016} {:answer/id #uuid "47c8c076-2cfe-513d-9669-c9bd6e8b5630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355017} {:answer/id #uuid "362267a0-7edb-515a-ac40-4e1b5d8c16bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355018} {:answer/id #uuid "1c365e42-283a-5021-95c4-f981ebb4cf91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355019} {:answer/id #uuid "270155cb-27cb-534e-96e2-082906379219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c8c076-2cfe-513d-9669-c9bd6e8b5630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355017} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d649628-4767-57ee-a5fc-c5f72a7961ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b754e6d1-17bd-5fb0-a3f2-f0423826f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-161273" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,v-u,\\,-2uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2v \\\\ 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-2uv} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\cdot ⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (2u+2v)+0\\cdot (2u+2v)+(v-u)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}-u{v}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{3}v-\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee20652e-ea25-5f53-84e1-6873e79a8558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355023} {:answer/id #uuid "c3640ffc-7ca5-577b-993e-a27b1d2d5416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355024} {:answer/id #uuid "f7854c32-21be-55b3-bc0c-12f44089aa1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355025} {:answer/id #uuid "504145a5-7a54-5817-9257-b968d41c8e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355026} {:answer/id #uuid "08e96c69-f2e4-5d74-bfa9-430dad51f79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7854c32-21be-55b3-bc0c-12f44089aa1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355025} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c7008d1-d51f-545e-9647-29e7cc5f4e45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15133e32-1381-5e6c-92d6-2b17486bef5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161306" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u{e}^{v},\\,u{e}^{-v},\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{e}^{v}+b{e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{-v},\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v},\\,-u{e}^{-v},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u{e}^{v}\\,y=u{e}^{-v}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩ \\\\  & =(u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{-v}+(u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{v}+u\\cdot (-2u) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{e}^{-v}+{u}^{2}+{e}^{v}-2{u}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{v}-{e}^{-v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot {e}^{v}+(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1-1=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d9fe6a-5772-5ebb-bd75-9a0073d09b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355030} {:answer/id #uuid "48c8aa06-d036-5bd8-a3ed-32ffad2c1e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355031} {:answer/id #uuid "5b11a934-68c7-5017-b89f-196e6c69ea42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355032} {:answer/id #uuid "502da1c2-083d-5404-bb32-83a3dadbf3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}+uv+2{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355033} {:answer/id #uuid "cbaba9fd-dca2-590e-a0fd-69c7a6e5403f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbaba9fd-dca2-590e-a0fd-69c7a6e5403f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355034} :answer-field/id #uuid "300c2456-ce6b-587b-a183-29ec768e2efc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd17085b-48fe-5be2-bc57-b62ce4e45b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161383" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,uv,\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y=uv\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =uv\\cdot v+uv\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot u \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
